r Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "8"} "1924 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/TEN'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Tennis at the 1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "20 September –  1 October 1988"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "4"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/660"} "Te-ni-seu-jang, Ol-lim-pik Gong-won, Seoul"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Tennis was contested at every Olympics from 1896-1924, but the sport was removed from the Olympic Program after the Paris Olympics. The sport was discontinued after 1924 because of disputes between the International Olympic Committee (IOC) and the International Lawn Tennis Federation (ILTF) over amateur rules. In addition, the ruling bodies of tennis, then centered in London, were concerned that the Olympic tournament might begin to overshadow Wimbledon."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Tennis would return as a demonstration sport in 1968 and 1984, and then return to the Olympic Program as a full-medal sport in 1988. Its return was orchestrated mostly by Italian IOC Member " [:a {:href "/athletes/899098"} "Giorgio De Stefani"] ", who had been President of the International Lawn Tennis Federation (ILTF) on three separate occasions. De Stefani was a former Italian doubles champion, reached the final of the 1932 French Championships in singles, losing to " [:a {:href "/athletes/8"} "Henri Cochet"] ", and played in 34 ties for the Italian Davis Cup team."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Seoul tennis events took place on hardcourts at the " [:a {:href "/venues/660"} "Te-ni-seu-jang"] ", or Olympic Tennis Centre, in the Olympic Park (Ol-lim-pik Gong-won) in Seoul. It was finished in 1986, being built specifically for the 1988 Olympics, and had 13 courts, with the main stadium having seating for 10,000."] "\n\n" [:p {} "There were four events in 1988 Olympic tennis, men’s and women’s singles and doubles. Eight nations won medals in 1988 tennis, with the United States winning the most, with 5, and winning both doubles events. The women’s singles was won by Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/124"} "Steffi Graf"] ", who had won the demonstration singles event at the 1984 Los Angeles Olympics."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/45037"} "Singles, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "20 – 30 September 1988"] "\n" [:td {} "64"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/45106"} "Doubles, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 September –  1 October 1988"] "\n" [:td {} "62"] "\n" [:td {} "31"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/45142"} "Singles, Women"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 September –  1 October 1988"] "\n" [:td {} "48"] "\n" [:td {} "26"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n"